  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Completion of the Master Plan and definition of a commercial Strategy for the Port of Guaymas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Completion of the Master Plan and definition of a commercial Strategy for the Port of Guaymas - Local Authorities (LAs) are important partners of the EU in the context of its development policy. NDICI-Global Europe has recognized them as key actors in advancing territorial approaches to local development and fostering local democracy. The action aims at the recognition of LAs as development actors per se and the establishment of an enabling environment for LAs that will allow them to deliver on their mandate and, in fine, improve the living conditions of their constituencies.The main activity of this action consists in the continuation of our engagement with i) global Associations of Local Authorities (ALAs) which have signed a framework partnership agreement with the EU in 2022, and ii) EU delegations to enhance their work with LAs. Direct support to sub-national authorities may also be considered in specific contexts.ALAs will thus continue their work to improve LAs&#xbf; capacities for dialogue at local, national, regional and global levels and EU delegations will be in a better position to enter into a constructive dialogue and support LAs and their associations in their respective countries. In addition, ALAs and EU delegations will reinforce LAs in sustainably delivering resilient services to their constituencies and facilitate their access to development finance. Grants will be awarded to global and regional ALAs and, potentially, to sub-national authorities to achieve the objectives above. The action may delegate funds to EU delegations in order for them to give grant to sub-national authorities. A service contract will be contracted to pursue the Territorial Approach to Local Development (TALD) facility&#xbf;s support to EU delegations to strengthen their work with LAs and their associations.</narrative>
  </description>
